ClassInitElimination took every invoked method's owner as initialized from then on, interface methods included. An
instance call proves its owner initialized only when the owner is a class: an instance exists, so its class and (with
patch 0010) its superclasses have been initialized. An interface is not initialized by the classes that implement it
on this target, so a later InitClass of that interface was deleted and its static fields read before its <clinit>.
mctick at FULL: HopperBlockEntity.suckInItems calls hopper.getLevelX() (Hopper), then inlines Hopper.getSuckAabb(),
whose InitClass Hopper went, so Hopper.SUCK_AABB was null: NullPointerException in AABB.move on the first hopper tick.
At ADVANCED getSuckAabb is not inlined (not used once), so its InitClass stayed in its own function. Instance calls
whose owner is an interface (or unknown) no longer count; static calls still do (a static method initializes its
class at entry).
Codegen: InitClass checks of interfaces after an interface call in the same method are kept.

